;; scope-ecall.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `scope-ecall.s` (P2-SCALAR.1).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py scope-ecall.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "scope-ecall.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `scope-ecall.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The expected observation is a REQUESTED trap, not a value — the same reason" "`smoke-trap` exists: a model that executes correctly and misreports the environment request is" "invisible to arithmetic-only differential testing. The trap step writes no register, and the" "run STOPS on it: the harness is told, and there is no guest handler to continue into.")
(expectations (program "scope-ecall.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 7") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000007"))) (derivation "An ordinary write, so the run has a step before the trap and the trap's position is observable.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn "ecall") (writes) (derivation "D-ECALL-EBREAK: ECALL causes a precise REQUESTED trap to the execution environment. It writes no register; the laboratory reports the typed environment-trap outcome to the harness and execution stops. The references observe cause 11 (environment call from M-mode) at the ecall's own address — the trap is reported ON the requesting instruction.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.8 (D-ECALL-EBREAK); RVI-INTRO, Exceptions/Traps/Interrupts (Requested Trap)")))
